.el .ds Aq '
.TH garuda-toolbox-maintenance-reset 1  "garuda-toolbox 6.3.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-maintenance\-reset \- Put programs\*(Aq settings back to Garuda\*(Aqs own, from /etc/skel. The replaced files are kept as backups beside them
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox maintenance reset\fR [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIENTRIES\fR> [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Put programs\*(Aq settings back to Garuda\*(Aqs own, from /etc/skel. The replaced files are kept as backups beside them
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Do not ask, carry the change out. Needed without a terminal
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the plan and stop, without asking and without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON Lines instead of text, for scripts. Needs `\-\-yes` or `\-\-dry\-run`
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIENTRIES\fR>
The settings, as `maintenance reset list` prints them
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-maintenance\-reset\-list(1)
List the settings that can be reset, with the files each replaces
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  garuda\-toolbox maintenance reset list
  garuda\-toolbox maintenance reset bash fish
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox\-maintenance(1), garuda\-toolbox(1)
